<p data-start="2774" data-end="2814">Layout is the foundation of good design.</p>
<p data-start="2816" data-end="2885">Even beautiful furniture won’t work if the arrangement feels awkward.</p>
<p data-start="2887" data-end="2916">Popular sitting room layouts:</p>
<p data-start="2918" data-end="3029"><strong data-start="2918" data-end="2940">Symmetrical layout</strong><br data-start="2940" data-end="2943" />Perfect for traditional homes. Sofas and chairs mirror each other for a balanced look.</p>
<p data-start="3031" data-end="3112"><strong data-start="3031" data-end="3051">L-shaped seating</strong><br data-start="3051" data-end="3054" />Great for open-plan living. Helps define the sitting area.</p>
<p data-start="3114" data-end="3194"><strong data-start="3114" data-end="3137">Conversation layout</strong><br data-start="3137" data-end="3140" />Chairs and sofas face inward, encouraging interaction.</p>
<p data-start="3196" data-end="3276"><strong data-start="3196" data-end="3214">Minimal layout</strong><br data-start="3214" data-end="3217" />Fewer pieces, more breathing room, ideal for modern homes.</p>
